<article class="env-example" id="0662">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0662">Example <span data-tag="0662">15.63.4</span>.</a> Let $K^\bullet , L^\bullet $ be objects of $D^{-}(R)$. Then there is a spectral sequence with </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  E_2^{p, q} = H^ p(K^\bullet \otimes _ R^{\mathbf{L}} H^ q(L^\bullet )) \Rightarrow H^{p + q}(K^\bullet \otimes _ R^{\mathbf{L}} L^\bullet )  \]
</div>
  <p> and another spectral sequence with </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  E_2^{p, q} = H^ p(H^ q(K^\bullet ) \otimes _ R^{\mathbf{L}} L^\bullet ) \Rightarrow H^{p + q}(K^\bullet \otimes _ R^{\mathbf{L}} L^\bullet )  \]
</div>
  <p> Both spectral sequences have $d_2^{p, q} : E_2^{p, q} \to E_2^{p + 2, q - 1}$. After replacing $K^\bullet $ and $L^\bullet $ by bounded above complexes of projectives, these spectral sequences are simply the two spectral sequences for computing the cohomology of $\text{Tot}(K^\bullet \otimes L^\bullet )$ discussed in Homology, Section <a href="/tag/012X" data-tag="012X">12.25</a>. </p>
</article>